<!--
  Completion graph caching, family O1.

  Reduced differential-fuzzing finding (seed 590). C2 is {a1,a0} and below C0; every C0 has an r1-predecessor in C2
  and r1 is functional. The consistency test merges blockable successors into a1 and a1 into a0 (a chain of
  merges). X = C0 and not C2 is unsatisfiable: an instance of X needs a C2 r1-predecessor, which is a0 or a1,
  and the functional r1 then forces the chain of merges again. The caching missed nodes that were merged into
  a node through a chain and the merge dependants of a node that was reactivated from the reactivation queue.
-->
